      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i'm looking at this house in seattle and the contract keeps mentioning \"escrow\" and an \"escrow agent\"... i'm a bit confused. what actually happens with the money while we're waiting to close? like who is holding it and why?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow, in a real estate transaction, is a process where a neutral third party holds funds and documents until all conditions of the sale are met. The escrow agent, who is typically a specialized company or attorney, acts as this trusted intermediary. They hold the money—like a big, secure holding pen—until the closing date, ensuring that the seller doesn't get paid until they hand over the keys, and the buyer doesn't hand over the final funds until the title is officially theirs. This protects both parties from the risk of the other party backing out.",
